<?php
return ['name' => 'empowered_ji_earth_the_nurturer', 'displayTitle' => ['en' => 'Empowered Ji Earth – The Nurturer', 'zh' => '身强己土'], 'locales' => ['en' => ['sections' => ['overview' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<p>Empowered Ji Earth is like rich, fertile soil that\'s been heavily watered – it\'s substantive, even a bit muddy and slow to shift. When its energy is strong, it tends to settle in one place and hold its ground firmly. This gives it incredible reliability and steadiness; it\'s the presence others trust to be consistent and supportive. However, too much heaviness can turn into stubbornness or stagnation if not careful. Its journey, therefore, is about transforming stubborn stillness into resilient strength. It learns to \'open channels for water to flow,\' finding ways to introduce flexibility and movement into its life. As The Anchor, Empowered Ji Earth provides a deep sense of security and stability to its environment, much like an anchor holding a ship steady. At the same time, Empowered Ji Earth knows when to pull up anchor and redirect inner resources, ensuring that its influence is not only stable but also adaptable and lasting.</p><p>Steady & Responsible: You are reliable to a fault. When you make a commitment, you uphold it with unwavering dedication. Hardworking and persistent, you don\'t shy away from long hours if that\'s what it takes to fulfill your duties. People see you as the rock of any group or project – you\'ll be there doing what needs to be done, thoroughly and patiently.<br/>Thorough & Detail-Oriented: Your mind is like fertile soil – it carefully processes and breaks down everything that\'s given to it. You consider all angles and plan meticulously. While this means your work and decisions are well-founded with few oversights, it also means you can become entangled in minor details or overly cautious. Sometimes you might miss the forest for the trees, or hesitate to seize a sudden opportunity because you\'re busy double-checking the plan.<br/>Stubborn at the Core: You have a warm, accommodating exterior – you\'re polite, often soft-spoken, and you avoid unnecessary conflict. But those who push you too far will quickly find that you have a hard inner core. Certain lines you simply will not cross, and if someone challenges your deeply held beliefs or tries to force you into a rushed change, you can become surprisingly firm and unyielding. This inner steel is one of your great strengths, but it can also isolate you if you\'re not open to compromise when needed.</p>'], 'love' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<p>Wood, Metal, Water. You have a solid foundation (Earth) and plenty of substance, but to be effective and efficient, you benefit from a dose of nimbleness and insight. Wood energy brings growth and new ideas, helping break up any overly rigid thinking. Metal brings clarity, precision, and the courage to cut out what doesn\'t work. Water introduces flow and adaptability, preventing you from becoming stuck. By integrating the qualities of Wood, Metal, and Water in your life, you enhance your flexibility and wisdom. This means your actions and decisions can become more efficient and well-timed, and you\'ll find it easier to connect with people and make the most of resources around you, rather than trying to do everything by sheer tenacity.</p>'], 'career' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<h4>Wealth</h4><p>You are the kind of person who benefits from growing within a stable platform. In practical terms, this means hitching yourself to an established institution or a mature industry and climbing steadily. You accumulate wealth best by being the dependable pillar in your workplace – promotions, raises, and bonuses come as you slowly but surely become invaluable to your organization. Quick in-and-out trades or speculative investments aren\'t really your style (nor to your advantage). You prefer sure bets, even if the returns are moderate, because you know consistency builds real wealth. Keep an eye on sectors related to land, natural resources, or commodities – these tangible areas align with your energy and can yield solid gains over time (e.g., investing in property, or companies dealing in metals, minerals, agriculture). Finally, when you do strike it rich in some venture, resist the temptation to keep doubling down; secure your gains (perhaps reinvest in safer long-term assets) and let your fortune gradually appreciate. You have good instincts for value – trust those, and avoid being swayed by the hype of \'easy money.\' Over a lifetime, your finances can become rock-solid, much like you.</p><h4>Health</h4><p>Your digestive health is crucial – treat your stomach and spleen well. Stick to a routine with meals; irregular eating or consuming too much cold/raw food can throw your system off balance. Favor warm, nourishing foods and don\'t overdo the spicy or greasy stuff, as tempting as it might be. Hydration and circulation are also themes for you: sometimes strong Earth energy leads to sluggish lymph or circulation. Make sure to drink plenty of water and get moderate exercise to keep things moving in your body. Even a brisk walk a few times a week can drastically improve your circulation and lymphatic health, which in turn boosts your immunity and overall vitality. Skin care is another area to note – perhaps surprisingly, your type can be prone to skin issues if stressed. Avoid overly processed or irritating foods that might cause inflammation. Keep your skin moisturized, and don\'t over-wash or strip your skin of natural oils (balance is key, as in all things). Adequate sleep and stress management will do wonders not just for your skin, but your entire well-being. Lastly, avoid being too sedentary; long hours in front of a computer without breaks can cause stiffness and reduce blood flow. Set a timer to stand up, stretch, or even do a few quick exercises every hour or two. These little habits ensure that your earthy strength remains vibrant and full of life rather than bogged down.</p><h4>Emotional Wellbeing</h4><p>Your mind is powerful, but it can sometimes become your own worst enemy when you get caught in loops of worry or internal debate. It\'s easy for you to sink into quiet overthinking, which can drain your spirit. To break out of that, look to physical activities that are immersive and somewhat intense – they\'ll help pull you out of your head. Swimming is excellent: when you\'re gliding through water, the sensation and rhythm force you to focus on your breath and body, not your thoughts, giving your mind a much-needed rest (and literally surrounding you with the Water element for balance!). Mountain climbing or hiking also does wonders. The effort of going up a slope, the fresh air, the expansive views at the top – all these remind you that the world is bigger than whatever might be looping in your mind. Additionally, being out in nature reconnects you to the broader perspective and can spark a gentle emotional release. Regularly scheduling such activities, even once or twice a month, will help clear mental blockages and prevent you from getting emotionally stuck. Over time, you\'ll learn that whenever you start feeling that heavy mental drag, it\'s a cue to move your body and engage with the natural elements; doing so will lift your mood and keep your emotions flowing in a healthy way.</p><h4>Career Pathways</h4><p>Where You Flourish: Management & Law: You excel in roles where careful management and adherence to rules are important. Positions like corporate manager or project supervisor suit you, as you provide steady leadership. You\'d also thrive as a lawyer, judge, or auditor – fields where meticulous analysis and precedent are valued. Once you commit to a company or institution, you tend to climb the ladder through sheer dependability and insight, making a name for yourself as someone who can handle weighty responsibilities without faltering. Finance & Commerce: Your practical and cautious nature is ideal for finance roles like banking, accounting, tax consultancy, insurance underwriting, or supply chain management. In these areas, slow growth, risk management, and consistency are rewarded – all things you\'re naturally good at. You could be the banking executive who builds client trust over decades, or the accountant everyone relies on for impeccable books. In international trade or supply chains, your systematic approach ensures goods and money flow smoothly, even in complex global operations. Technology & Engineering: Fields that involve methodical problem-solving and incremental progress suit you well. Think data analyst, systems engineer, geologist, or quality assurance engineer. You\'re the person who can dig into a pile of data or a drawn-out engineering challenge and steadily work it out. Your patience and thoroughness mean you catch mistakes others miss and refine processes to make them rock-solid. These roles also let you contribute to large projects (like building infrastructure or developing software) where your piece might be painstaking, but it\'s absolutely critical to the success of the whole. Creative Strategy & Consulting: You might also find a niche in strategy roles that require deep thinking and long-term vision. As a strategic consultant, urban planner, or even an author/scholar, you can delve into a subject, research it thoroughly, and produce comprehensive plans or works. For instance, as a city planner or architect, your designs might not be the flashiest, but they stand the test of time and account for every practical detail. As a writer or academic, you could create important, enduring work by building your ideas brick by brick. Transportation & Logistics: Managing systems that require reliability and timing, like a logistics network, public transportation scheduling, or airline operations, could be a good fit. You have the patience to coordinate moving parts and the foresight to prepare for contingencies. Whether it\'s running a delivery fleet, optimizing supply warehouses, or coordinating flights and crews, you bring order to complexity. People may not see your work directly, but they experience the efficiency and reliability you orchestrate behind the scenes. Where Energy Feels Drained: Real Estate Speculation & Construction Entrepreneurship: While you do well in stable roles within these fields, being the front-line entrepreneur or developer can be fraught with too many uncertainties – something that would stress you greatly. Markets that boom and bust, dealing with contractors who might cut corners, and needing to make aggressive deals quickly could all clash with your careful nature. You\'d rather build one solid house than gamble on ten. Academic Teaching & Research (entry-level): Surprising as it might sound, certain education roles could frustrate you, especially if bureaucracy or slow progress hampers the impact you want to have. Entry-level teaching may involve a lot of red tape and changing educational trends, which can be hard to keep up with if you\'ve developed a fixed method. Similarly, research positions that require constant publishing and chasing grants (with their fickle competitiveness) might make you uncomfortable. You prefer scholarly work that\'s steady and respected, not the churn of proving yourself repeatedly in a cutthroat academic environment. Clerical & Secretarial Work: Routine administrative tasks that offer no challenge or growth can feel like a quagmire for you. While you can do them exceptionally well, if there\'s no path for advancement or enrichment, you might feel stuck and underutilized. You\'re meant to handle bigger responsibilities than just filing or data entry all day. Without a sense of progression or ability to improve systems, such jobs could sap your motivation.</p>'], 'relationship_friends' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Geng Metal: Geng Metal helps break rigid thinking patterns and enhances adaptability while boosting efficiency.</li><li>Ren Water: Ren Water\'s flowing nature quietly nourishes your spirit, easing melancholy and harmonizing relationships.</li></ul>'], 'relationship_couple' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Xin Metal: Xin Metal partners spur progress, enhancing life enjoyment and wealth creativity.</li><li>Gui Water: Gui Water partners silently nurture you, resolving overly principled tendencies and promoting emotional communication.</li></ul>'], 'celebrities_international' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Audrey Hepburn: An Academy Award-winning actress who was also renowned for her humanitarian work. Audrey carried an air of grace and reliability, devoting her later years to UNICEF efforts in a steady, hands-on way. She demonstrated how one can be a consistent beacon of kindness and style, influencing the world not with flashiness, but with enduring class and compassion – much like Empowered Ji Earth\'s quiet influence</li><li>Emmeline Pankhurst: A British political activist and leader of the suffragette movement. Emmeline\'s steadfast pursuit of women\'s voting rights, through years of organization and even personal sacrifice, exemplifies the tenacity and principle of The Anchor. She was immovable on her core belief and ultimately helped achieve a revolutionary change through persistent effort</li><li>Charles Darwin: The scientist who formulated the theory of evolution. Darwin spent decades gathering data, observing nature, and carefully working through his ideas before presenting them to the world. His methodical, thorough approach and the monumental impact of his work (which fundamentally anchored modern biology) mirror Empowered Ji Earth\'s pattern of slow, meticulous labor yielding world-changing results</li><li>Sigmund Freud: The founding father of psychoanalysis, who explored the depths of the human psyche. Freud\'s work was groundbreaking, but it was built on years of careful case studies and theoretical development. He held firm to his theories, even when controversial, and his persistence carved out an entire new field of psychology. This blend of stubborn conviction and deep introspection resonates with your energy</li><li>Carl Gustav Jung: A prominent psychiatrist and protege of Freud who later founded analytical psychology. Jung introduced concepts like the \'collective unconscious\' and archetypes, and his influence spans psychology, philosophy, and even arts and literature. He exemplified Empowered Ji Earth by collecting wisdom from various cultures, mythologies, and experiences, integrating them into a stable framework of ideas. Jung was deeply principled and somewhat private, focusing on the work over personal glory, much like how you operate behind the scenes to create lasting impact</li></ul>'], 'celebrities_domestic' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Ding Lei: The founder of NetEase, one of China\'s biggest tech companies. Ding Lei is known for his consistent and pragmatic leadership style, quietly building NetEase into a diverse and solid enterprise (games, music, education) over the years. He tends to avoid the limelight and focuses on steady growth and product quality. His reliable, no-fuss approach to tech entrepreneurship embodies the steadfast Anchor energy</li><li>Yu Qiuyu: A famous essayist and cultural scholar in China. Yu Qiuyu is known for his reflective writings on culture and history, often bridging classical wisdom with modern reflection. He has maintained a steady voice in the literary world over decades, influencing readers through thoughtful, well-grounded works rather than sensationalism. His role as a keeper of culture and reason is akin to the Anchor\'s role in society</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_dailytips' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Savor Some Sour: Introduce a bit of sour flavor into your daily diet – it\'s surprisingly fortifying for you. Enjoying a glass of lemon water in the morning, adding a splash of vinegar to your meals, or snacking on yogurt or citrus fruits can help regulate your digestion and lift your energy. In the Five Elements theory, sour corresponds to Wood energy, which nourishes Earth. It\'s a small, tasty way to keep your system in balance and your mind sharp</li><li>Flowing Water Imagery: Use visuals of flowing water to remind you to stay adaptable. Setting your phone or desktop wallpaper to a serene waterfall, a river, or ocean waves can have a calming, subconscious effect. Each time you see those gentle currents, you\'ll be prompted to let go of stress and allow things to move naturally. It\'s a subtle cue that while you are anchored, you can also sway and adapt like a boat riding gentle waves</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_color' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Green (Wood): Green is the color of growth, renewal, and flexibility. It helps break up any mental logjams you experience and keeps your perspective fresh and open. Try incorporating more green around you: perhaps wear clothing in olive or emerald tones, keep potted plants nearby, or even use green stationery. This color infuses your life with a sense of vitality and possibility, ensuring you don\'t get too set in your ways.</li><li>Turquoise (Wood): Turquoise (or cyan/teal) carries a similar Wood energy with an added emphasis on communication and harmony. It\'s excellent for lubricating social interactions and fostering cooperation. You might use a turquoise mug at work or a teal-colored notebook for important meetings – these subtle accents can help conversations flow more smoothly. Turquoise also has a calming, uplifting vibe, easing tension in group settings (or within yourself).</li><li>Black & Blue (Water): The colors of depth and intuition. For Empowered Ji Earth, these shades awaken insight and sharpen your instincts, helping you stay flexible and magnetic in social and business worlds. Surround yourself with navy, cobalt, or sleek black accents to unlock wisdom, adaptability, and abundance.</li><li>White (Metal): White brings clarity, structure, and discernment. It amplifies your natural ability to assess risks and make sound decisions. Using white elements – maybe a white lamp on your desk, white bedsheets, or even wearing a white shirt during critical tasks – can heighten your focus and give you a sense of order amidst complexity. White is like a mental spotlight, helping you see the path in confusing times and reinforcing your confidence in navigating complicated environments.</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_location' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>East (Wood): The East is all about new beginnings, innovation, and breaking through. Facing east when you need a creative breakthrough or are considering a major decision can stimulate your mind. Eastern energy encourages you to think outside the box and supports any initiative where you must step out of your comfort zone. If you\'re planning something like a career move or a big project, try meditating or brainstorming while oriented to the east – you may find fresh ideas germinating more readily and the courage to make a bold move growing.</li><li>West (Metal): West is the direction of completion, gathering, and harvesting resources. When you focus westward, you harness energy that helps you organize and consolidate. If you have disparate resources or ideas and need to pull them together to achieve a goal, work facing west or spend time in the western part of your home/office. This can symbolically aid you in efficiently integrating all the pieces at your disposal. West also attracts helpful people and opportunities that align with your objectives, ensuring you have the support and materials you need to succeed.</li><li>North (Water): North represents connectivity, wisdom, and fluidity. By facing north, you draw on energies that enhance your networking luck and your ability to get support from others. This is great when you\'re trying to build a team, seek mentorship, or rally friends around a cause. North helps you reach out and receive assistance gracefully, reminding you that asking for help or delegating can be a strength, not a weakness. It keeps your journey smooth by ensuring you\'re not pulling the weight all alone – a critical balance for an Anchor personality like yours.</li></ul>']]], 'zh' => ['sections' => ['overview' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<p>己土为湿润之土，身强则土性淤滞，容易固守一方而缺乏流动性。然而，这份厚重也带来可靠与稳健。</p><p>稳重务实：行事踏实，注重承诺与责任，具备持久耐力。<br/>思维缜密：考虑周全，但易陷入细节纠缠，过分求稳可能错失良机。<br/>内核坚守：表面敦厚包容，实则暗藏固执，触及底线时显现强硬内核。</p>'], 'love' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<p>身强己土，喜用神为木、金、水。己土如沃土，身强时根基厚实，但有时容易固化思维或行动拘谨。</p>'], 'career' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<h4>财富运势</h4><p>适合深耕职场，抱紧平台的大腿稳赚。避免快进快出式投资。关注土地、矿产、大宗商品领域。</p><h4>健康隐患</h4><p>调理脾胃，避免油腻食物，少吃生冷，保持饮食清淡；促进淋巴循环，适量运动，多喝水；改善皮肤代谢；避免久坐不动。</p><h4>情绪管理</h4><p>容易陷入精神内耗，可通过游泳、登山等活动调节。</p><h4>职业管理</h4><p>推荐行业：建筑工程：建筑施工、工程管理、工程造价。仓储物流：物流管理、仓储运营、供应链。贵金属加工：金、银、珠宝、工艺品。供应链管理：采购、供应、物流、渠道管理。社区养老服务：养老院、社区服务、健康管理。二手资产交易：二手车、二手家具、回收利用。行政管理：行政事务、人事管理、办公管理。园林师：园林设计、景观规划、园艺。市政设施维护：城市管理、公共设施、市政工程。慎重行业：直播电商：直播带货、电商平台、网红经济。新媒体：公众号、网站、社交媒体。旅游业：旅行社、旅游景区、旅游服务。活动策划：活动组织、庆典策划、市场营销。危机公关：危机处理、公关管理、品牌维护。销售：销售代理、商业销售、服务销售。</p>'], 'relationship_friends' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>庚金：庚金可以打破你的思维定势，让你从多角度思考问题。</li><li>壬水：壬水的流动可以带动你，让你在面对事情时更加变通。</li></ul>'], 'relationship_couple' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>辛金：辛金可以打破你的拖延固化的思维模式。</li><li>癸水：癸水能更好地滋养你，让你能没有负担地表达自己的情感。</li></ul>'], 'celebrities_international' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Emmeline Pankhurst：英国女权运动领袖，通过激进抗议推动女性选举权实现</li><li>Charles Darwin：提出进化论</li><li>Sigmund Freud：精神分析学派创始人，探索潜意识理论，革新人类对心理疾病的认知</li><li>Carl Gustav Jung：分析心理学创始人，提出\'集体无意识\'概念，影响现代心理治疗与神话研究</li></ul>'], 'celebrities_domestic' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>丁磊：网易创始人</li><li>巩俐：国际影星，担任联合国粮食大使</li><li>余秋雨：作家</li><li>朱婷：女排奥运冠军</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_dailytips' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>多吃酸味的食物</li><li>手机壁纸可以用流水图</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_color' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>绿色（木）：绿色象征生长与活力，能帮助己土打破固化思维。</li><li>青色（木）：青色带来流通与协调的力量，能润滑人际关系。</li><li>白色（金）：白色象征清晰与理智，能增强风险把控意识。</li><li>黑色 / 蓝色（水）：蓝色/黑色有助于增强洞察力与商业头脑。</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_location' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>东方（木）：东方的能量象征生长与突破，利于做出突破性决策。</li><li>西方（金）：西方的能量能帮助资源重组与聚合。</li><li>北方（水）：北方的能量象征流动与人际，利于拓展人脉。</li></ul>']]]], 'version' => 1];
